  "intuition": "Simplified the loss by removing the learnable margin_coef and entropy_scale for stability and clarity. Kept the key preference signal alpha * scale * (log_prob_w - log_prob_l) and added a fixed scaled cost_gap penalty. Clamped the logits between -20 and 20 to ensure numerical stability. Removed entropy_gap to avoid introducing instability or invalid expects. This preserves the preference semantics while ensuring required keys in expects and stabilizing training.",
  "pseudocode": "x = alpha * scale * (log_prob_w - log_prob_l) - beta * cost_gap\nx = clamp(x, -20, 20)\nloss = sum(-logsigmoid(x) * weight)",
  "hyperparams": {
